.TH GIT-PR-STACK 1 "2026-06-13" "git-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-pr-stack \- discover a linear GitHub pull request stack
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git pr-stack
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ number|url|branch ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git pr-stack
discovers the linear GitHub pull request stack connected to a target pull
request and prints it in parent-to-child order. Without a target, it uses the
pull request for the current branch.
.PP
A stack is connected when one pull request's base branch is another pull
request's head branch. If a stack branches into multiple child pull requests,
contains a cycle, or has multiple same-repository parent heads, the command
stops instead of guessing a landing order.
.PP
URL targets must belong to the current GitHub repository. Discovery requests a
201st sentinel record and fails closed when more than 200 pull requests are
open, rather than returning a truncated stack.
.PP
Repository identity is derived with ambient GH_REPO and GH_HOST routing
removed. List, view, and checks requests are pinned to that exact host and
owner/repository, and every returned canonical pull request URL is validated.
.PP
Each structured record must have matching pull request numbers and canonical
URLs, exact boolean fields, well-formed head and base refs, and a head repository
consistent with its cross-repository flag. Its head OID must be a canonical
40- or 64-digit lowercase hexadecimal value. Explicit numeric and URL targets
must resolve to the same pull request number. Branch targets must resolve back
to the exact head branch.
The independently viewed target must also match its inventory topology;
concurrent retargeting aborts discovery.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-porcelain
Print one stable tab-separated schema-v1 record per pull request. Its nine
columns remain kind, index, number, base, head, ready, reason, checks, and URL.
.TP
.B \-\-porcelain=v2
Print a stable schema-v2 record. V2 appends head OID, structured head repository,
and cross-repository flag to the nine schema-v1 columns.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Stack printed.
.TP
.B 1
Stack could not be read or has ambiguous, branched, or cyclic topology.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or local environment error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-pr-ready (1),
.BR git-pr-restack (1),
.BR git-pr-land-stack (1)
